<section class="live-edit">
    <div class="live-edit-row">
        <div class="live-edit-label">
            <h2>Live edit Steam games</h2>
            <p>
                Writes launch options and Proton builds straight into the running Steam client, so
                a save takes effect at once. Without it every save has to close Steam, edit the
                files it owns, and start it again.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="live-edit-control">
            @if (IsLoading)
            {
                <span class="control-note">Checking…</span>
            }
            else if (!State.IsSteamInstalled)
            {
                <span class="control-note is-warning">No Steam installation found.</span>
            }
            else
            {
                <label class="switch">
                    <input type="checkbox"
                           checked="@State.IsEnabled"
                           disabled="@IsBusy"
                           @onchange="OnToggledAsync"/>
                    <span>@StatusLabel</span>
                </label>
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="explanation">
        Steam offers this only when it finds an empty <code>.cef-enable-remote-debugging</code>
        file in its own directory as it starts, so switching it on or off restarts Steam. It opens
        a port on this machine that any program running as you can use to drive Steam. Other Steam
        add-ons, such as Decky Loader, use the same file, and turning this off removes it for them
        as well.
    </p>

    @if (State.MarkerPath is not null)
    {
        <p class="marker-path" title="@State.MarkerPath">@PathDisplay.Abbreviate(State.MarkerPath)</p>
    }

    @if (Unsettled is not null)
    {
        <p class="message is-warning">@Unsettled</p>
    }

    @if (Message is not null)
    {
        <p class="message @(Failed ? "is-error" : "is-success")">@Message</p>
    }
</section>
